# Environment - the real file this project actually loads is `.env`
# (see myproject/settings.py's read_env(BASE_DIR / ".env") call);
# ".eee" only ever appears in code comments as an in-joke name for it,
# never as a real path, so it ignored nothing and .env (real DB
# password + LLM API keys) ended up committed. Never re-add a filename
# here without checking it against settings.py's actual read_env() call.
.env

